window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-e13354c6b025f6aa"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"control-your-dot\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"dot\">控制 dot</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>内置安全措施、现有应用权限和自动审批检查会从一开始就生效。你可以查看进行中的工作、补充指示，或设置可选的自定义规则。</p> <p><a id=\"review-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">查看工作进度</h2> <p>在桌面应用中打开 dot 的个人资料，然后选择 <strong>活动（Activity）</strong>。选择一项任务即可查看其进度、文件和结果，包括正在后台进行的工作。如果任务正在等待你作出决定、连接应用、登录或批准操作，请打开请求并作出回应，以便继续。工作进行期间，你仍可以调整方向。</p> <p>打开 <strong>已安排（Scheduled）</strong> 可查看 dot 的定时任务。请核对任务指示、执行时间和结果发送位置。有关重复任务，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2\">任务与记忆</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"how-action-review-works\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">操作审核机制</h2> <p>dot 执行可能影响账户或分享信息的操作前，系统会自动根据你的指示、权限、自定义规则和内置安全要求进行审核。审核结果会决定操作能否继续、是否需要你批准，或是否有步骤必须由你亲自完成。例如，更改密码必须由你本人操作。</p> <p>给持续性指示设定清晰范围：谁可以参与、应该做什么，以及何时执行。让 dot 起草回复，并不意味着授权它发送回复。明确指示可以涵盖该范围内今后的操作；超出范围的操作则需要另行决定。</p> <p>dot 还可以研究你已连接应用中的信息，寻找可提供帮助的方式。用于研究的工具不能发送消息、修改应用内容，也不能控制你的浏览器或电脑。任何后续操作仍受相同的权限和安全要求约束。</p> <p><a id=\"set-custom-rules\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">设置自定义规则</h2> <p>自定义规则是用于设定具体长期边界的可选控制。先在对话中清楚说明指示即可；不必为每次审批都创建一条规则。</p> <p>设置好 dot 后，请根据你使用的应用打开自定义规则：</p> <ul> <li><strong>桌面版和网页版：</strong>打开 <strong>设置（Settings）</strong> &gt; <strong>个性化（Personalization）</strong>，然后在 <strong>权限（Permissions）</strong> 下选择 <strong>自定义规则（Custom rules）</strong>。</li> <li><strong>iOS 和 Android：</strong>打开侧边栏，然后选择 <strong>自定义（Customize）</strong> &gt; <strong>自定义规则（Custom rules）</strong>。</li> </ul> <p>选择 <strong>添加（Add）</strong>，描述操作，并选择 dot 应如何处理，然后选择 <strong>添加规则（Add rule）</strong>。可选项如下：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>规则选项</th> <th>作用说明</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>无需询问，直接执行</td> <td>无需请求批准即可执行指定操作。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>你明确要求时才执行</td> <td>只有你明确提出该操作时才继续；否则会在执行前立即询问。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>执行前先询问</td> <td>执行指定操作前先征求批准。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>交由你处理</td> <td>请你亲自执行该操作。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>例如，可以为向客户发送消息选择 <strong>执行前先询问（Ask before taking action）</strong>，为删除共享项目文件选择 <strong>交由你处理（Hand off to you）</strong>。对于写作风格、你希望如何接收进度更新等偏好，可在对话中说明；自定义规则则用于控制 dot 何时可以执行操作。</p> <p>已保存的自定义规则适用于同一账户中的 dot。规则可以允许 dot 执行特定操作、要求它先向你确认，或禁止它执行某项操作。dot 会尽量遵循这些指示，但仍可能出错。规则不会授予它访问应用或电脑的权限，也不能覆盖内置安全要求或免除必要确认（例如使用已保存的登录信息前的确认）。</p> <p>使用规则菜单即可编辑或删除规则。选择 <strong>打开插件（Open Plugins）</strong> 可查看 <strong>插件权限（Plugin permissions）</strong>；插件权限与自定义规则相互独立，用于控制应用操作。如果工作区管理员禁用了自定义规则，你将无法编辑已保存的规则，而且这些规则不会生效。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa?anchor=for-workspace-admins\">配置 dots 权限</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"for-workspace-admins\"></a></p> <p><strong>工作区管理员请注意：</strong> 工作区权限、设置以及安全与治理指引，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46\">为工作启用 dots</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"manage-data-settings\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">管理数据设置</h2> <p>ChatGPT 数据控制也适用于符合条件的 dot 对话以及它执行的工作。OpenAI 不会直接使用主动研究内容或 dot 的私密笔记训练模型。如果研究信息进入符合条件的对话或任务，则适用你的数据设置。请参阅 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/7730893-data-controls-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT 中的数据控制（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"stop-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">停止工作</h2> <p>暂停 dot、停止已委派的任务以及取消日程安排，产生的效果各不相同：</p> <ul> <li><strong>暂停（Pause）</strong> 会停止 dot 当前的主要任务，但不会停止所有已委派任务，也不会取消未来的定时运行。</li> <li>在 <strong>活动（Activity）</strong> 中打开已委派任务，可查看并停止该任务。</li> <li>打开 <strong>已安排（Scheduled）</strong>，禁用或删除你想结束的重复任务。</li> </ul> <p>使用 <strong>继续（Resume）</strong> 可让暂停的 dot 恢复工作。停止工作不会撤销已完成的操作。请分别检查正在运行的任务和已安排的日程。</p> <p><a id=\"reset-your-dot\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"delete-your-dot\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"dot_1\">删除 dot</h2> <p>使用 <strong>删除（Delete）</strong> 删除 dot。请先阅读确认信息，了解删除操作如何处理对话、记忆和定时任务。确认前保存你需要的结果；此操作无法撤销。</p> <p>删除 dot 不会撤销它在已连接应用中完成的更改，也不能收回已经发送给其他人的消息。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"control-your-dot\">Control your dot</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Built-in safeguards, existing app permissions, and automatic approval checks apply from the start. You can review ongoing work, add instructions, or set optional custom rules.</p> <h2 id=\"review-work\">Review work</h2> <p>In the desktop app, open your dot's profile and select <strong>Activity</strong>. Select a task to review its progress, files, and results, including work happening in the background. If it's waiting for a decision, app connection, sign-in, or approval, open the request and respond to continue. You can change direction as work continues.</p> <p>Open <strong>Scheduled</strong> to review your dot's scheduled tasks. Check the task's instructions, timing, and destination. See <a href=\"#/article/a-9ffa6664dba73aa2\">tasks and memory</a> for recurring work.</p> <h2 id=\"how-action-review-works\">How action review works</h2> <p>Before your dot takes an action that could affect your accounts or share information, an automatic review checks it against your instructions, permissions, custom rules, and built-in safety requirements. The review determines whether the action can proceed, needs your approval, or includes a step you must do yourself. For example, you must change a password yourself.</p> <p>Give ongoing instructions a clear scope: who can take part, what should happen, and when. Asking your dot to draft replies doesn't give it permission to send them. A specific instruction can cover future actions within that scope; an action outside it needs another decision.</p> <p>Your dot can also research information from apps you've connected to look for ways to help. The tools it uses for that research can't send messages, change app content, or control your browser or computer. Any follow-up action is subject to the same permissions and safety requirements.</p> <h2 id=\"set-custom-rules\">Set custom rules</h2> <p>Custom rules are optional controls for specific ongoing boundaries. Start with clear instructions in your conversation; you don’t need to create a rule for every approval.</p> <p>After setting up your dot, open custom rules for your app:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Desktop and web:</strong> Open <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Personalization</strong> and select <strong>Custom rules</strong> under <strong>Permissions</strong>.</li> <li><strong>iOS and Android:</strong> Open the sidebar, then select <strong>Customize</strong> &gt; <strong>Custom rules</strong>.</li> </ul> <p>Select <strong>Add</strong>, describe the action, choose how your dot should handle it, and select <strong>Add rule</strong>. The choices are:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Rule</th> <th>Intended behavior</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Take action without asking</td> <td>Take the specified action without asking for approval.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Take action when you say so</td> <td>Proceed when you explicitly request the action; otherwise ask immediately before acting.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Ask before taking action</td> <td>Ask for approval before taking the specified action.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Hand off to you</td> <td>Ask you to take the action instead.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>For example, you could choose <strong>Ask before taking action</strong> for sending messages to customers, or <strong>Hand off to you</strong> for deleting shared project files. Use your conversation for preferences such as writing style or how you like updates; custom rules control when your dot can take an action.</p> <p>Saved custom rules apply to your dot in the same account. They can give your dot permission for particular actions, require it to check with you, or prevent it from taking an action. They are instructions your dot tries to follow, and it can make mistakes. They don't grant access to an app or computer, override built-in safety requirements, or remove required confirmations such as approval to use a saved login.</p> <p>Use a rule's menu to edit or delete it. Select <strong>Open Plugins</strong> to review <strong>Plugin permissions</strong>, which control app actions separately from custom rules. If your workspace disables custom rules, you can't edit saved rules, and they don't apply. See <a href=\"#/article/a-e13354c6b025f6aa?anchor=for-workspace-admins\">Configure dots permissions</a>.</p> <p><a id=\"for-workspace-admins\"></a></p> <p><strong>For workspace admins:</strong> See <a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46\">Set up dots for work</a> for workspace permissions, setup, and security and governance guidance.</p> <h2 id=\"manage-data-settings\">Manage data settings</h2> <p>Your ChatGPT data controls also apply to eligible conversations with your dot and the work it carries out. OpenAI doesn't train models directly on proactive research or its private notes. If information from that research becomes part of an eligible conversation or task, your data settings apply. See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/7730893-data-controls-in-chatgpt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">data controls in ChatGPT (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"stop-work\">Stop work</h2> <p>Pausing your dot, stopping a delegated task, and canceling a schedule have different effects:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Pause</strong> stops your dot's current main task. It doesn't stop every delegated task or cancel future scheduled runs.</li> <li>Open a delegated task in <strong>Activity</strong> to inspect and stop that task.</li> <li>Open <strong>Scheduled</strong> to disable or delete the recurring task you want to end.</li> </ul> <p>Use <strong>Resume</strong> to continue a paused dot. Stopping work doesn't undo completed actions. Review active tasks and schedules separately.</p> <p><a id=\"reset-your-dot\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"delete-your-dot\">Delete your dot</h2> <p>Use <strong>Delete</strong> to delete your dot. Read the confirmation for how deletion handles conversations, memories, and scheduled tasks. Save any results you need before confirming; the action cannot be undone.</p> <p>Deleting your dot doesn’t undo changes already made in connected apps or recall messages already delivered to other people.</p>"};
